        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to recall the root श्रथ in the curadi class, which carries the sense of दौर्बल्ये (weakness/looseness) per the Dhatupatha, though I'm also considering whether it's listed under प्रयत्ने or मोक्षणे in different readings of the curadi gana.\n\nActually I now recall the relevant line is in the kathādi (adanta) group of curadi roots: \"सार कृप श्रथ दौर्बल्ये.\" Since श्रथ belongs here as an adanta root, the final अ gets elided without triggering upadhā vṛddhi, giving श्रथयति, and the vidhiliṅ form श्रथयेत्.\n\n",
